I have here a server with an LSI SCSI card.  On one channel is a tape =20
changer, on the other an external RAID5 box with a number of disks in. =20
  All worked fine until a recent upgrade and now the disk array is not =20
recognised.

The disk array is still recognised on machine startup in the SCSI card =20
output on HBA 1, ID 0, LUN 0.  The tape changer is recognised in the =20
new install and has the correct devices assigned as before.

The SCSI card used for the tape changer and disk array is an LSI Logic =20
card.  The MegaRAID is seperate, a Dell PERC which has the system =20
disks attached.  However, another PERC was tested instead of the LSI =20
SCSI card which had the same problem.

lspci:
00:02.0 PCI bridge: Intel Corporation E7525/E7520/E7320 PCI Express =20
Port A (rev 09)
00:04.0 PCI bridge: Intel Corporation E7525/E7520 PCI Express Port B (rev 09=
)
)
02:0c.0 SCSI storage controller: LSI Logic / Symbios Logic 53c1030 =20
PCI-X Fusion-MPT Dual Ultra320 SCSI (rev 07)
02:0c.1 SCSI storage controller: LSI Logic / Symbios Logic 53c1030 =20
PCI-X Fusion-MPT Dual Ultra320 SCSI (rev 07)
02:0e.0 RAID bus controller: Dell PowerEdge Expandable RAID controller =20
4 (rev 06)

On the old install, the following is seen:

/proc/scsi/sg/device_strs
PE/PV   =091x2 SCSI BP     =091.0
MegaRAID=09LD 0 RAID1  286G=09516A
E1600SR =09                =090001 (the disk array)
HL-DT-ST=09RW/DVD GCC-4243N=09A102

uname -a:
Linux ubuntu 2.6.20-15-generic #2 SMP Sun Apr 15 07:36:31 UTC 2007 =20
i686 GNU/Linux


On the new install:

/proc/scsi/sg/device_strs
HL-DT-ST=09RW/DVD GCC-4243N=09A102
PE/PV   =091x2 SCSI BP     =091.0
MegaRAID=09LD 0 RAID1  286G=09516A

uname -a:
Linux ubuntu 2.6.22-14-server #1 SMP Sun Oct 14 23:34:23 GMT 2007 i686 =20
GNU/Linux

dmesg output from both builds is attached to this message.

A livecd of the old OS still recognises the disk array as sdb1 correctly.

Is this an issue with modules/options or a problem with the distro =20
(Ubuntu server)?

Regards,

David


